.TH tufold n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tufold
.PP
\fBtufold\fR folds long lines to a fixed width, similar to Unix \fBfold\fR.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tufold

puts [::tclutils::tufold::text $text -width 80]
puts [::tclutils::tufold::file README.md -width 72 -words 1]
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tufold::foldLine line ?options?
::tclutils::tufold::text text ?options?
::tclutils::tufold::file path ?options?
.CE
.SS Options
.CS
-width n           maximum line width, default 80
-words boolean     prefer breaking at blanks when possible
.CE
.PP
\fB\-words 1\fR is a small convenience mode. It is not a full formatter. A line longer than \fB\-width\fR is broken at the last blank at or before column \fB\-width\fR+1. The blanks at the break are dropped: trailing blanks of the line and leading blanks of the next one. A word longer than \fB\-width\fR is cut hard.
.PP
Difference from Unix \fBfold \-s\fR: \fBfold \-s\fR keeps the blanks, breaks after the last blank within the width and keeps leading blanks of the next line. For \fB"ab   cd"\fR with width 3, \fBfold \-s\fR gives \fB"ab "\fR, \fB"  "\fR, \fB"cd"\fR; \fBtufold\fR gives \fBab\fR, \fBcd\fR.
.SS Errors
.PP
\fB\-width\fR not a positive integer raises \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON INTEGER \-width}\fR, \fB\-words\fR not a boolean \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-words}\fR, an unknown option \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION \-name}\fR.
.SS "Line ends"
.PP
\fBtext\fR and \fBfile\fR return text that ends with LF exactly when the input does: \fB"b\enJörg\en"\fR gives a result with final LF, \fB"b\enJörg"\fR one without, like \fBtuhead\fR, \fBtutail\fR and \fBtunl\fR. Versions before 0.3 dropped the final LF.
